1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,363
I remembered every payment. The
collector remembered the ones that let

2
00:00:04,363 --> 00:00:05,950
him charge us again.

3
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:11,104
Rain had soaked his ledger before we
reached the lodge. Our balance looked

4
00:00:11,104 --> 00:00:12,690
like a blue cloud.

5
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:17,443
He tapped the blank space and demanded
double. Jason spread the pages

6
00:00:17,443 --> 00:00:19,820
under the lamp, seeking our number.

7
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:25,770
I let the man talk. Each explanation
gave me time to find the entry he

8
00:00:25,770 --> 00:00:26,960
hoped I'd forgotten.

9
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:31,718
Three pages earlier, my signature sat
beneath a payment, dry. He had

10
00:00:31,718 --> 00:00:33,700
counted the same debt twice.

11
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:38,057
Jason moved both entries into the light.
The collector stopped explaining.

12
00:00:38,057 --> 00:00:40,830
I waited until he offered a receipt.

13
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:46,383
He crossed out our balance and signed.
We left his ruined ledger behind. I

14
00:00:46,383 --> 00:00:47,970
kept the receipt flat.

15
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:52,196
Outside, Jason asked whether I'd
remembered that payment. Of course.

16
00:00:52,196 --> 00:00:56,000
People always get generous when they
call me forgetful.
